────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Modified third-party code
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The compiled engine WASM binary does not use upstream ttf-parser 0.25.1 verbatim:
it is built against the copy in vendor/ttf-parser/, which fixes the loca and
gvar offset handling for fonts with exactly 65535 glyphs (the released code
drops those tables, silently erasing every glyph outline; the loca fix is a
backport of an unreleased upstream commit, and gvar gets the same treatment).
The fixes and their rationale are documented in vendor/ttf-parser/README-PATCH.md
in the source repository (https://github.com/zakideee/boundsvg).
ttf-parser is MIT OR Apache-2.0 (no attribution obligation beyond this notice);
this entry exists so that the provenance of the shipped binary is explicit.


